{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790962351,"nonce":"zCeWOqwIagbv9s4m+fz3hINl564=","title":"Components need an owner scope","message":"Div and Text take the tree as their last constructor argument, which every\ntemplate would have to thread through. A SolidJS-style owner, the current\ntree and owner set while a component renders, removes the parameter and\ngives a component's bindings and computeds a definite disposal point when it\nunmounts (onCleanup), instead of waiting for GC finalizers. Disposal needs\nBlinc to dispose signals and computeds first (see the issue on releasing\nthem from the graph).","files":null}]}